@startuml standalone_run
title paddock run: a session in the terminal it was typed in (SPEC section 11)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

legend top
  No herdr anywhere. The process that asked becomes the sandbox, so what
  would have been a pane is the terminal the user was already sitting in.
endlegend

actor User
participant "cli.py" as CLI
participant "tui.py\n(the chooser)" as TUI
participant "standalone.py" as Standalone
participant "sessions.py" as Sessions
participant "backends/srt.py\nbackends/microsandbox.py" as Backend
participant "the run dir\nlaunch.sh, shell.sh, run.sh" as RunDir
participant "the sandbox\nsrt process / msb microVM" as Sandbox

User -> CLI : paddock run [profile] [--backend]
activate CLI

alt no profile named
  CLI -> TUI : choose(cwd)
  TUI --> CLI : one plan: local | attach | new session
  note right : no terminal to draw in is an error here,\nexactly as it is for `paddock`
end

alt the plan is a local tab
  CLI --> User : "you already have a terminal", exit 0
  note right : there is no herdr to open a tab in
else the plan is a session to attach to
  CLI -> Standalone : attach(session, shell)
  Standalone -> Sessions : attach_standalone(session)
  Sessions -> Backend : load_run(run_dir), then ensure_live(run)
  Backend --> Sessions : the run, its scripts rewritten if stale
  note right : a sandbox that has gone ends the session here,\nthe same answer a tab gets.
  note right : no pane id is registered, so what closing\nherdr's last tab means is left as it was
else the plan is a new session
  CLI -> Standalone : start(profile, backend, keep_alive)
  Standalone -> Sessions : prepare_standalone(profile, backend)
  Sessions -> Backend : prepare(profile)
  Sessions -> RunDir : standalone.pid: the process\nthat is about to become this run
  Backend -> RunDir : settings / shim dir / config dir,\nlaunch.sh and shell.sh
  Backend --> Sessions : the run, and a vm_handle if it has one

  alt the run leaves nothing running (srt)
    Sessions --> Standalone : script + workdir, no session
    note right : ephemeral: no registry entry.\nstandalone.pid is what stops a sweep\ntaking the run dir from under it
  else the run leaves a microVM (msb)
    Sessions -> Sessions : register the session,\nno pane ids
    Sessions --> Standalone : script + workdir + session
    Standalone -> Sessions : wrap_standalone(here, collect argv)
    Sessions -> RunDir : write run.sh:\nlaunch.sh, then `paddock collect <session>`,\nunder a trap for ctrl-c and HUP
  end
end

Standalone -> Standalone : chdir(workdir)
Standalone -> Sandbox : execv(/bin/sh, <run dir>/run.sh or launch.sh)
deactivate CLI
note right
  The process is replaced here. The failure hold,
  the pane log and the policy are the launch
  script's, so they are the same as in a pane.
end note

activate Sandbox
User -> Sandbox : works in the sandbox, then exits
Sandbox -> CLI : run.sh only: `paddock collect <session>`
deactivate Sandbox
activate CLI
CLI -> Sessions : forget(session)
Sessions -> Backend : collect(run_dir, vm_handle)
Backend -> Sandbox : msb rm -f <handle>
CLI --> User : "collected <name>"
deactivate CLI

note over Sessions
  A session with no panes survives reconciliation, so a
  paddock in another terminal cannot collect a run that
  is under way. Its VM is claimed, so a gc leaves it alone.
end note

@enduml
